course: dictionary
lesson: 15007
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Reservation» is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues.
explain: «We made a reservation for four people at seven o'clock.» Here a reservation is a booking, a table kept just for you. Ask yourself: what would fit? A table kept for us fits, and a doubt does not.
explain: «I have reservations about the plan, because it looks far too risky.» Here reservations means doubts. The clues are «about the plan» and «too risky», so the speaker is not sure the plan is a good idea.
fact: Reservation has several meanings, so always check the context.
fact: A reservation can be a booking, such as a table at a restaurant or a room in a hotel.
fact: A reservation can be a doubt you have about something.
fact: In the USA and Canada, a reservation is land kept for Native American peoples.
fact: In the UK, the central reservation is the strip in the middle of a motorway. Phrases to learn: make a reservation, without reservation, have reservations about.
exercise: «We need to make a reservation at the restaurant before Saturday.» What does reservation mean here? | A small picture on a menu | A doubt about the food | A strip of grass in the middle of a road | *A booking, a table kept for you
exercise: «Mum has reservations about going out on the boat in such rough sea.» What does reservations mean? | The middle of the road | *Doubts | Lots of tickets | Bookings for seats
exercise: The car drove along the motorway, and the grass in the middle was the central reservation. Where is the central reservation? | In the hotel room | *In the middle of the motorway, between the lanes | Inside a shop | At the side of the sea
test: «She accepted the job without reservation.» What does without reservation suggest? | Without any pay | Only for one day | *Fully and happily, with no doubts | Unwillingly, with a long sigh
test: In our history lesson we learned that a reservation is land kept for Native American peoples in the USA. Which meaning is this? | A strip in the middle of a motorway | *Land kept for Native American peoples | A doubt about something | A booking for a table
exam: «The hotel found my reservation, so we got the room we wanted.» What does reservation mean here? | A doubt about the room | A map of the hotel | A strip of land in the middle of a road | *A booking
